# LIGHT GLITTER: the light a Mirror sends to its crystal store - small golden sparks that fly along the beam to the
# crystal and twinkle on the way. Drawn through ParticleSystem::emitStream (the game's StructureSystem::drawLightLinks),
# which places the emitter on a beam for a frame and sets `Life` from the beam's length: so `Rate` is 0 and `Life` is
# unused here. `Speed` is the flight speed along the beam (m/s).
# Colors are linear HDR (rgb * intensity); the scene tonemaps, so bright additive values glow.
ParticleEffect LightGlitter
	Emitter Glitter
		Texture Textures/Particles/spark.dds
		Rate 0
		SpawnRadius 0.3
		ConeAngle 1.5
		Speed 6.5 8.5
		Life 1 1
		Gravity 0
		Drag 0
		Turbulence 1.2 0.8 0.5
		Size 0.11 0.05
		SizeVariance 0.6
		VelocityStretch 0.02
		ColorStart 9.0, 6.5, 2.2, 1
		ColorEnd 6.0, 3.6, 0.9, 0
		Additivity 1
		FadeIn 0.05
		FadeOutStart 0.85
		SoftFade 0.1
